# Cache Components runtime APIs

`cacheComponents: true` is on. Keep it on.

Never call `cookies()`, `headers()`, or `connection()` in:

- `getRequestConfig` (`i18n/request.ts`)
- the root layout shell (`<html>` / `<body>`)

Those reads must live in a child wrapped in `<Suspense fallback={...}>`.

Never wrap `cookies()` / `headers()` / `connection()` in `"use cache"`.

```ts
// BAD — blocks prerender of every route
export default getRequestConfig(async () => {
  const store = await cookies()
  return { locale: store.get("locale")?.value || "es" }
})

// GOOD — static locale (this app is es-only)
export default getRequestConfig(async () => ({
  locale: "es",
  messages: { ...(await import("./email-validator/es.json")).default },
}))
```

Dynamic `params` / `searchParams`: keep the page/layout sync; await the promise inside a Suspense child.

Do not use `export const instant = false` unless the user explicitly asks.
